{"kind":"chart","id":"ch/vix0jqxo","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":70,"top":190,"width":700,"height":400},"name":"","chartType":"bar","title":"Error terms retained for PNA"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/3kyutg","slideIndex":4,"text":"At the middle noise setting, the learned model included 78 candidate error terms. SLC kept 53 for mitigation and set a bounded bias limit of 0.05. This reduced local PNA preprocessing from about 1.29 seconds to 1.13 seconds. The sampling-cost estimate fell from about 2.61 to 1.92."}
