{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lkfqpsb2","slideIndex":7,"position":{"left":72,"top":397,"width":1020,"height":66},"text":"It dropped low-impact error terms and lowered the estimated sampling cost, with a small allowed bias.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/kj6pwnuh","slideIndex":7,"position":{"left":72,"top":512,"width":720,"height":40},"text":"Next step for a hardware-ready result","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#8A3FFC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7mx8r2t8","slideIndex":7,"position":{"left":72,"top":561,"width":1060,"height":62},"text":"Connect NoiseLearnerV3 to an IBM Quantum backend, then rerun the same workflow with measured rates.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/v47s04","slideIndex":7,"text":"The local results show the algorithmic flow but are not hardware results because calibration rates are synthetic. The official assignment asks for NoiseLearnerV3 and a simulated noisy backend; official documentation says NoiseLearnerV3 does not have a local testing mode. If an IBM Quantum account and backend become available, replace the synthetic model with the output of the official noise learner. Source: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives"}